@*
    The middle column: the kind pills, and the rows of the open slice newest
    first under three headings — Today, This week, Older than a week — each
    with its count. Nothing is typed here — a thought typed at the desk goes in
    through the header's capture field, which is the pane's, so the column only
    ever reads what the state holds.

    The pills are a filter and the kind pills multi-select: pressing "Video"
    and "Article" shows both. "All", first, carries the slice's count and is
    the pressed pill while no kind is; pressing it clears the kinds. Each kind
    carries its count from before the filter, so the numbers do not shift as
    pills are pressed. A kind with no rows in the slice has no pill — a pill
    that would show nothing is a pill that lies.

    A row is four things: a tile with the kind's mark, the title, a line saying
    what kind of thing it is and where it came from ("Article · Web clipper"),
    and how long ago it arrived. The kind is always a word as well as a mark,
    because shape alone is not a carrier. A row whose item has a rule-based
    suggestion the reader has not turned down says "suggested" under its age,
    so the rows worth a second look stand out before they are opened. Tags and
    repositories are the detail's, not the row's. A routed row stays and says
    so; an archived one has left.

    Rows are buttons, because choosing one is the act. aria-pressed carries the
    selection, and the row's own classes carry the border-and-strip look that
    .devbook/design/interaction-guidelines.md#focus-and-selection asks for — distinct
    from hover and from focus.

    Picking several is a second, separate selection: Select, at the end of the
    pills, puts a box beside
    every row, Shift extends from the last box pressed, and InboxBulkBar acts on
    what is picked. The chosen row (the detail) and the picked rows (the bar)
    are independent, as they are in the Tasks list.

    A list open in the column has one act of its own beside Select: Move list
    to backlog, which routes every open row of the list as one batch. Two or
    more rows open the Before you route panel (InboxRoutePanel), the same one
    the bulk bar's Move to backlog opens; a list of one asks a plain confirm,
    because there is nothing to order. The list is left standing; only what it
    held goes.

    The rows also hear the digits that take the chosen item's suggestions, so a
    reader who has just clicked a row can take "2" without moving focus to the
    detail. Only the rows: the bulk bar above them has fields of its own.
*@

<div class="inbox-pane__column inbox-pane__column--list" data-testid="inbox-pane-column-list">
    @if (!State.Loaded)
    {
        @* Local-first, so this is usually on screen for a frame — but the snapshot
           is still a read away, and a list on its way is drawn in the shape of one
           rather than as nothing (.devbook/design/interaction-guidelines.md,
           Loading States). Nothing is there for a reader to tell from a list that
           failed to draw. Hidden in one piece, like every skeleton. *@
        <div class="inbox-pane__loading" data-testid="inbox-loading" aria-hidden="true">
            @foreach (var width in SkeletonWidths)
            {
                <Skeleton Shape="SkeletonShape.Block" Width="@width" />
            }
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        var kinds = State.KindCounts;

        @if (kinds.Count > 0)
        {
            @* Select sits with the pills because both are about which rows the
               column is showing; it turns the boxes on, the way the Tasks pane's
               Select chip does, so a column read rather than acted on stays free
               of them. *@
            <div class="inbox-pane__toolbar">
                <div class="inbox-pane__filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by kind" data-testid="inbox-pane-filters">
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="@(State.KindFilter.Count == 0)"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => State.ClearKindFilter()"
                                  BaseClass="inbox-pane__pill"
                                  PressedCssClass="inbox-pane__pill--pressed"
                                  Title="Show every kind"
                                  TestId="inbox-kind-all">
                        <span class="inbox-pane__chip-label">All</span>
                        <Badge BaseClass="inbox-pane__chip-count" Kind="" TestId="inbox-kind-all-count">@State.SliceItems.Count</Badge>
                    </ToggleButton>
                    @foreach (var kind in kinds)
                    {
                        <ToggleButton Pressed="@State.KindFilter.Contains(kind.Slug)"
                                      PressedChanged="_ => State.ToggleKind(kind.Slug)"
                                      BaseClass="inbox-pane__pill"
                                      PressedCssClass="inbox-pane__pill--pressed"
                                      Title="@($"Show only {kind.Label.ToLowerInvariant()} items")"
                                      TestId="@($"inbox-kind-{kind.Slug}")">
                            <span class="inbox-pane__chip-label">@kind.Label</span>
                            <Badge BaseClass="inbox-pane__chip-count" Kind="" TestId="@($"inbox-kind-{kind.Slug}-count")">@kind.Count</Badge>
                        </ToggleButton>
                    }
                </div>
                <div class="inbox-pane__modes">
                    @if (State.SelectedListId is not null && !State.DeferredSelected)
                    {
                        @* A list's own act: route what it still holds open as one
                           batch, one plan named after it. Asks first, because it
                           acts on every open row at once and cannot be undone. *@
                        var open = State.ListOpenItems.Count;
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                   Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                   CssClass="inbox-pane__list-to-backlog"
                                   Disabled="@(open == 0 || State.RoutingInFlight)"
                                   Title="@(open == 0
                                       ? $"Nothing open in {State.SliceName} to move."
                                       : $"Route the {InboxDesktopState.Counted(open, "open item", "open items")} here to the backlog as one plan")"
                                   OnClick="() => State.AskListRouteAsync()"
                                   TestId="inbox-list-to-backlog">Move list to backlog</AppButton>
                    }
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="@State.SelectionMode"
                                  PressedChanged="on => State.SetSelectionMode(on)"
                                  BaseClass="inbox-pane__pill inbox-pane__pill--ghost"
                                  PressedCssClass="inbox-pane__pill--pressed"
                                  CssClass="inbox-pane__select-toggle"
                                  Title="@(State.SelectionMode ? "Stop picking items" : "Pick items to act on together (x)")"
                                  TestId="inbox-select-toggle">Select <kbd class="inbox-pane__key" aria-hidden="true">X</kbd></ToggleButton>
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        @if (State.SelectionMode)
        {
            <InboxBulkBar State="@State" />
        }

        <ConfirmDialog Open="@State.ListRouteConfirmOpen"
                       Title="Move this list to the backlog?"
                       Message="@ListRouteMessage"
                       ConfirmText="Move to backlog"
                       OnConfirm="OnListRouteConfirmedAsync"
                       OnCancel="State.CancelListRouteConfirm"
                       TestId="inbox-list-to-backlog-dialog"
                       ConfirmTestId="inbox-list-to-backlog-confirm"
                       CancelTestId="inbox-list-to-backlog-cancel" />

        <InboxRoutePanel State="@State" />

        var groups = State.VisibleGroups;

        @if (groups.Count == 0)
        {
            @if (State.FilteredOut)
            {
                <EmptyState Title="@($"No {FilteredKindsLabel()} items in {State.SliceName}")"
                            Description="The pills above are hiding every row here."
                            BaseClass="empty-state inbox-pane__empty-state"
                            TestId="inbox-pane-empty"
                            data-inbox-empty="filtered">
                    <Action>
                        <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small" OnClick="() => State.ClearKindFilter()" TestId="inbox-empty-clear">Show all kinds</AppButton>
                    </Action>
                </EmptyState>
            }
            else if (State.SelectedListId is not null)
            {
                <EmptyState Title="@($"Nothing in {State.SliceName}")"
                            Description="Open an item and choose Move to list to file it here."
                            BaseClass="empty-state inbox-pane__empty-state"
                            TestId="inbox-pane-empty"
                            data-inbox-empty="list" />
            }
            else
            {
                <EmptyState Title="Nothing captured yet"
                            Description="Write one down in the field above, or capture one from your phone — it lands here on the next sync."
                            BaseClass="empty-state inbox-pane__empty-state"
                            TestId="inbox-pane-empty"
                            data-inbox-empty="first-use" />
            }
        }
        else
        {
            @* One list with the group headings inside it, so the rows stay one
               run a reader steps through with j and k, and one landmark named
               after the slice. The Deferred slice runs in the order its items
               come back, so it has no age headings. *@
            <ul class="inbox-pane__list" aria-label="@State.SliceName" data-testid="inbox-pane-list" @onkeydown="OnShortcutKeyAsync">
                @foreach (var group in groups)
                {
                    @if (!State.DeferredSelected)
                    {
                        <li class="inbox-pane__group" role="presentation" @key="@($"group:{group.Key}")" data-testid="@($"inbox-group-{group.Key}")">
                            <h3 class="inbox-pane__group-title">@group.Label <span class="inbox-pane__group-total" data-testid="@($"inbox-group-{group.Key}-count")">· @group.Items.Count</span></h3>
                        </li>
                    }
                    @foreach (var item in group.Items)
                    {
                        @Row(item)
                    }
                }
            </ul>
        }
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The first load's placeholder rows, of differing length so that
    /// they read as rows rather than as a pattern.</summary>
    private static readonly string[] SkeletonWidths = ["100%", "92%", "96%", "88%"];

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public InboxDesktopState State { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The count and the plan the batch will become. The tag's digits
    /// are minted by the module when it routes, so the preview shows the slug
    /// and leaves them out. Deferred items stay behind in the list, and when
    /// there are any the sentence says so.</summary>
    private string ListRouteMessage =>
        $"Move {InboxDesktopState.Counted(State.ListOpenItems.Count, "open item", "open items")} of {State.SliceName} "
        + $"to the backlog as one plan tagged {InboxPlanTag.Preview(State.SliceName)}? The list stays"
        + State.ListDeferredCount switch
        {
            0 => ".",
            1 => "; its 1 deferred item stays with it.",
            var deferred => $"; its {deferred} deferred items stay with it.",
        };

    private Task OnListRouteConfirmedAsync() => State.RouteListToBacklogAsync();

    /// <summary>One row: the box beside it while picking, then the row itself —
    /// the kind's tile, the title over "kind · source", and the age with the
    /// "suggested" and "Routed" markers under it.</summary>
    private RenderFragment Row(InboxItemDto item) => @<text>
        @{
            var selected = item.Id == State.SelectedItemId;
            var picked = State.IsPicked(item.Id);
            var open = item.Status is InboxStatus.Unprocessed or InboxStatus.Deferred;
        }
        <li class="@(picked ? "inbox-pane__item inbox-pane__item--picked" : "inbox-pane__item")"
            @key="item.Id"
            data-inbox-kind="@item.KindSlug"
            data-testid="inbox-pane-item">
            @if (State.SelectionMode)
            {
                @* Beside the row rather than in it: the row is a button,
                   and a box inside a button is a control nobody can reach.
                   Heard on click rather than on change, as the task row's
                   gutter is, because Shift is what turns a press into a
                   range and only a mouse event carries it. *@
                <span class="inbox-pane__gutter">
                    <Checkbox Checked="@picked"
                              CssClass="inbox-pane__pick"
                              TestId="@($"inbox-pick-{item.Id:D}")"
                              aria-label="@($"Select {Title(item)}")"
                              @onclick="e => State.TogglePicked(item.Id, !picked, e.ShiftKey)" />
                </span>
            }
            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                       BaseClass="inbox-pane__row"
                       CssClass="@(selected ? "inbox-pane__row--selected" : null)"
                       OnClick="() => State.SelectItem(item.Id)"
                       TestId="@($"inbox-item-{item.Id:D}")"
                       id="@RowId(item.Id)"
                       aria-pressed="@(selected ? "true" : "false")">
                @* The kind's mark on a tile. aria-hidden, because the word is on
                   the line below; a kind this build does not know has no mark
                   and the tile stays empty rather than guessing. *@
                <span class="inbox-pane__kind-tile" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="inbox-pane-item-tile">
                    <CaptureKindMarker Value="@item.KindSlug" CssClass="inbox-pane__kind-mark" />
                </span>
                <span class="inbox-pane__row-body">
                    <span class="inbox-pane__row-title" data-testid="inbox-pane-item-title">@Title(item)</span>
                    <span class="inbox-pane__row-meta">
                        <span class="inbox-pane__kind" data-testid="inbox-pane-item-kind">@InboxLabels.Kind(item.KindSlug)</span>
                        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                        <span class="inbox-pane__source"
                              title="@($"Captured via {InboxLabels.Channel(item.Channel)}")"
                              data-testid="inbox-pane-item-source">@InboxLabels.Channel(item.Channel)</span>
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Person))
                        {
                            <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                            <span class="inbox-pane__person" data-testid="inbox-pane-item-person">shared by @TagText.Display(item.Person)</span>
                        }
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="inbox-pane__row-end">
                    <time class="inbox-pane__row-age"
                          datetime="@item.CapturedAt.ToString("O")"
                          title="@item.CapturedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("f", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)"
                          data-testid="inbox-pane-item-age">@State.Age(item.CapturedAt)</time>
                    @if (open && State.HasSuggestions(item.Id))
                    {
                        <Badge BaseClass="inbox-pane__suggested"
                               Kind=""
                               Title="Classification has a suggestion for this item"
                               TestId="inbox-pane-item-suggested">suggested</Badge>
                    }
                    @if (item.Status == InboxStatus.Triaged)
                    {
                        <Badge BaseClass="inbox-pane__routed" Kind="" TestId="inbox-pane-item-routed">@InboxLabels.Status(item.Status)</Badge>
                    }
                </span>
            </AppButton>
        </li>
    </text>;

    /// <summary>Reads which rows have a suggestion to mark, whenever the list's
    /// parameters are set. A no-op once every open row on screen has its answer
    /// for the current snapshot.</summary>
    protected override Task OnParametersSetAsync() => State.LoadRowSuggestionsAsync();

    /// <summary>A bare digit takes the chosen item's suggestion with that number,
    /// as it does in the detail.</summary>
    private Task OnShortcutKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) =>
        e.CtrlKey || e.AltKey || e.MetaKey || e.ShiftKey ? Task.CompletedTask : State.AcceptShortcutAsync(e.Key);

    /// <summary>A row's element id, so the pane can put the focus back on the
    /// row a keyboard step or a triage session ended on.</summary>
    public static string RowId(Guid id) => $"inbox-row-{id:D}";

    private static string Title(InboxItemDto item) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Title) ? "Untitled" : item.Title;

    /// <summary>The pressed kinds as one phrase — "video", or "video or article"
    /// — for the filtered-empty title.</summary>
    private string FilteredKindsLabel()
    {
        var labels = State.KindFilter
            .Select(slug => InboxLabels.Kind(slug).ToLowerInvariant())
            .OrderBy(label => label, StringComparer.Ordinal)
            .ToList();

        return labels.Count switch
        {
            0 => "such",
            1 => labels[0],
            _ => string.Join(", ", labels[..^1]) + " or " + labels[^1]
        };
    }
}
